Jesus' family lineage
This is the genealogy of the family of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David. He is also the son of Abraham.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah, in his ancestors, divides them into two groups, distinguished by the name of two persons among his ancestors. So, Judah is the ancestor of Abu 'Abd al-'Aziz and Uzayr. Tamar is the mother of 'Abd al-'Aziz and Uzayr, Barzah. 'Abd al-'Aziz is the ancestor of Hazun and Ram. Hazun is the ancestor of Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Solomon was the father of Boaz. Rahab was the mother of Boaz. Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
And Jesse was the father of King David. David was the father of Solomon. Solomon's mother was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
Asa is the father of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat is the father of Jehoram. Jehoram is the father of Ahaziah. Ahaziah is the father of Joash. Joash is the father of Amaziah. Amaziah is the father of Azariah. Azariah is the father of Jotham. Jotham is the father of Ahaz. Ahaz is the father of Hezekiah. Hezekiah is the father of Manasseh. Manasseh is the father of Amon. Amon is the father of Josiah. Josiah is the father of Jehoiakim. Jehoiakim is the father of Jehoiachin. Jehoiachin is the father of Zedekiah. Zedekiah is the father of Seraiah. Seraiah is the father of Amariah. Amariah is the father of Ahitub. Ahitub is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Ahimelech. Ahimelech is the father of Abiathar. Abiathar is the father of Zadok.
Uzaziya was the father of Ya'qub. And Ya'qub was the father of Uziyya. And Uziyya was the father of Ahmar. And Ahmar was the father of Hayzam.
Hashkakiyyah, the breakfaster was Mansuh. Mansuh was the breakfaster Amun. Amun was the breakfaster Yusha'iyah.
And Joshua fathered Ibzan, and his brothers, in those days. And in those days, the Jewish people were exiled to Babylon.
After that, the family line continued. Jeroam was the father of Shallum. Shallum was the father of Zibiah.
Zerubbabel was the father of Abiud. Abiud was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azor.
Azur was the father of Zadu. Zadu was the father of Akim. Akim was the father of Eliud.
Eliud is the father of Eliezer. Eliezer is the father of Matthan. Matthan is the father of Jacob.
Jacob is the father of Joseph. Joseph is the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
From Abraham, peace be upon him, to David, peace be upon him, there were fourteen (14) generations. From David, peace be upon him, until the time when the Children of Israel were forced to go to Babylon, there were fourteen (14) generations. From that time until the Messiah, peace be upon him, there were fourteen (14) generations. The Messiah, Jesus, the son of Mary, peace be upon them, was born.
This is how the birth of Jesus Christ came about. His mother was Mary and Joseph had promised to marry her. But before they began to live together, it became clear that she would have a child. She became pregnant through the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband, Yusuf, was a devout man. He did not wish to publicly shame her. Therefore, he planned to quietly divorce her.
But while Joseph was pondering these things, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. And the angel said, "Joseph, son of David, do not fear to take Mary your wife into your home. For the child who is conceived in her is of the Holy Spirit."
She will have a child. You must name him Jesus. And that is because he will save his people from their sins."
All this has happened to lead to what the Lord said would happen. He said it through the prophet,
The virgin will conceive a child. She will give birth to a son. And this son will be called Emmanuel." (Isaiah 7:14) The name Emmanuel means "God with us."
Joseph woke up. He did what the angel of the Lord commanded him. He took Mary into his house as his wife.
But he did not have marital relations with her until after she gave birth to a son. And Joseph gave him the name Jesus.
The wise men visit Jesus.
Jesus was born in Bethlehem in the land of Judah. This happened while Herod was king over the land of Judah. And after Jesus was born, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem.
They asked, "Where is the child who has been born to be king of the Jews? For we have seen his star in the east and have come to worship him."
When King Herod heard this, he was deeply disturbed, and everyone in Jerusalem was also disturbed.
And Herod called together all the chief priests and the rulers of the people from among the children of Israel. And he called for the wise men who were in his kingdom. And he said to them, "Go and search for the young child, and when you have found him bring me word, so that I may also go and pay him homage." When they had heard the king they departed, and behold, the star which they had seen at its rising went before them until it came to rest over the place where the young child was. When they saw the star they rejoiced exceedingly with great joy. And when they had come to the house where the young child was, they fell down before him and offered him homage. And then, being warned in a dream not to return to Herod, they departed for their own country by another way. And Joseph arose and took the young child and his mother by night and departed for Egypt. And they remained there until the death of Herod, that what the Lord had said through the prophet might be fulfilled, "Out of Egypt I called my son." Then Herod, when he saw that he had been tricked by the wise men, was infuriated, and he sent and killed all the male children in Bethlehem and in all its districts, from two years old down, according to the time which he had ascertained from the wise men. Then was fulfilled what was spoken by the prophet Jeremiah, "A voice was heard in Ramah, lamentation and great weeping, Rachel weeping for her children and refusing to be comforted, because her children were no more." (Matthew 2:1-18)
He said, "This is what the prophet wrote, and he said, '
"But a house for you, in the land of Judah. They are without doubt the least important among the cities of Judah. A ruler will come out from you. He will be the shepherd of my people Israel."
Then Herod secretly called the wise men. And they told him secretly the time from which they came to worship him by the stars.
He sent them to a house they had. And he said: "Go! And consider the souls by finding. And by merely finding him, inform me. And I, I come to him to worship him as he said."
After the wise men had listened to the king, they departed on their way. As for the star that they had seen when they were in the East, it went before them. And in the end, this star stopped above the place where the child was.
When they saw the star, they were overwhelmed with joy.
The wise men went to the house. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They bowed down before him and honored him. Then they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
But God warned them in a dream not to return to Herod. So they returned to their own country by another route. The flight into Egypt of the family of Jesus
When the wise men had gone, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream. The angel said, "Get up! Take the child and his mother and escape to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you. Herod will search for the child to kill him."
Joseph got up. During the night, he left for Egypt with the child and his mother Mary.
They stayed there until King Herod died. In this way, the words of the Lord spoken by the prophet were fulfilled. He had said, "I have indeed brought my son out of Egypt." (Hosea 11:1)
Herod realized that the wise men had deceived him. He became very angry. He issued orders regarding Bethlehem and the surrounding area. All boys aged two years and under were to be killed. This coincided with the time the wise men saw the star.
In this way, the words of the prophet Jeremiah were fulfilled. For he had said,
A voice is heard in Ramah, lamenting and mourning deeply. Rachel weeps for her children, refusing to be comforted because they are gone." (Jeremiah 31:15) The family of Jesus returns to Nazareth.
After Herod's death, Joseph saw a dream while he was still in Egypt. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him.
The angel said, "Rise! Take the child and his mother. Go to the land of Israel. Those who were trying to kill the child are dead."
Joseph got up. He took the child and his mother Mary, returning to the land of Israel.
But then he heard that Archelaus was king of Judea. Archelaus was ruling in place of his father Herod. This made Joseph afraid to go there. After being warned in a dream, Joseph returned to the land of Galilee instead.
He has this, and that he was living in a city called Nazareth. And with that, the word of the prophets about the Messiah was fulfilled. For they said: "He will be called a Nazarene."
John the Baptist is preparing the way.
In those days John the Baptist came, preaching in the wilderness of Judea.
He said, "Repent of your sins! For the kingdom of heaven is at hand."
John is the one the prophet Isaiah spoke about. He said, "A voice of one calling in the desert, 'Prepare the way for the Lord; make his paths straight.' " (Isaiah 40:3)
John's clothes were made of camel's hair. He had a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.
The people came out to him from Jerusalem and all of Judea, and they also came from all of the region of the Jordan.
When they acknowledged their error, John baptized them in the Jordan River.
John saw many Pharisees and Sadducees coming to where he was baptizing. He said to them, "You are like a den of poisonous snakes! Who warned you to flee from the coming wrath?"
Bear fruit that shows you have distanced yourself from your sins.
Do not suppose that you can say to yourselves, 'Abraham is our father.' I say to you, God is able from these stones to raise up children to Abraham.
The axe is already laid at the roots of the trees. All trees that do not bear good fruit will be cut down. They will be hewn and thrown into the fire.
I baptize you with water, calling you to repentance for the forgiveness of your sins. But after me, one is coming who is mightier than I. I am not worthy to carry his sandals. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit.
His pitchfork is in his hand to clear the straw from his threshing floor. He will gather his wheat into the storeroom. But he will burn up the husks with fire that can't be put out." Jesus Is Baptized
Jesus came from Galilee to the River Jordan. He wanted to be baptized by John.
But John tried to stop him. He said to Jesus, "I need to be baptized by you. So why are you coming to me?"
Jesus answered, "Let it be so now. It is fitting for us to do this. It fulfills the holy plan of God." Then John agreed.
And behold, the heavens were opened when the Lord Jesus Christ came up out of the water, and at that moment they saw the divine manifestation. The Lord Jesus Christ saw the Spirit of God descending upon Him like a dove.
And behold, a voice from heaven said: "This is my Son, whom I love; with him I am well pleased."
Temptation of Jesus
The Holy Spirit led Jesus into the desert. There, the devil tempted him.
After forty days and forty nights without food, Jesus felt hungry.
Indeed, the temptation came to him. And he said, "If you are the Son of God, command that these stones become bread."
Jesus answered, "It is written, 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'" (Deuteronomy 8:3)
Then the devil took Jesus to the holy city. And he made him stand on the highest point of the temple.
"If you are the Son of God," he said, "throw yourself down. For it is written: 'He will command his angels concerning you, to guard you carefully; he will rescue you from the lion's mouth and from the horn of the wild ox.' " (Psalm 91:11,12)
Jesus answered, saying, "It is written also, 'You shall not tempt the Lord your God.'" (Deuteronomy 6:16)
Finally, the devil took Jesus to a very high mountain. And he showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory.
"If you bow down and stand humbly, you say to me: 'I will give you all of this,' he said that."
Jesus said to him, "Get behind me, Satan! For it is written: 'Worship the Lord your God, and serve him only.' " (Deuteronomy 6:13)
Then the devil left Jesus. And angels came and took care of him. Jesus begins to preach.
John had been imprisoned. When Jesus heard about this, he returned to Galilee.
Jesus left Nazareth. He went to live in the town of Capernaum. This was beside the lake in the region of Zebulun and Naphtali.
In that way, it has borne out what the prophet Isaiah said. He said,
Land of Zebulun! Land of Naphtali! Galilee, where non-Jews dwell. Land along the Mediterranean Sea! Territory east of the Jordan River!
They will see a great light. For they are now living in a very dark land. But a light will shine for them." (Isaiah 9:1,2)
From that time on, Jesus began to preach, saying, "Turn away from your sins!" He also said, "The kingdom of heaven is near." After this, Jesus chose the first disciples.
One day, Jesus was walking by the Sea of Galilee. There, he saw two brothers. They were Simon Peter and his brother James (son of Zebedee). They were casting a net into the lake. They were fishermen.
"Hello. Follow me," said Jesus. "I will make you fishers of men."
Immediately they left their nets and followed him.
Leaving there, he saw two other brothers. They were James, the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. They were in a boat with their father Zebedee. As they were preparing their nets, Jesus called to them.
Immediately they left the boat and their father and followed Jesus. Jesus heals the sick.
Jesus went throughout Galilee. There he taught in the synagogues. He preached the good news of God's kingdom. He healed every disease and illness the people had.
His news spread throughout Syria. People brought him all who were sick with various diseases. Some were suffering from severe pain. Others were possessed by demons. Some were shaking violently. Others were completely unable to move. Jesus healed all these.
Large crowds followed him. Some people from the village of Galilee, and from the region known as the Ten Cities, and from Jerusalem and Judea, came. Some of them came from the region across the Jordan River.
Christ bestows blessings.
Jesus saw the crowds. Therefore he went up to a mountain and sat down. His disciples came to him.
Then he began to teach them. And he said,
Blessed are the meek, for the kingdom of heaven belongs to them.
Yes, those who mourn will be comforted.
Blessed are the free from pride, for they shall inherit the earth.
Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for what is right. They will be filled.
Blessed are those who wrong. And they will continue to wrong.
They are the blessed ones, whose hearts you describe as pure. Indeed, they will see God.
Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called children of God.
Blessed are those who suffer for doing what is right. The Kingdom of Heaven belongs to them.
Blessed are you when people insult you, persecute you, and falsely say all kinds of evil against you because of me.
Rejoice and be glad. Your reward in heaven is great. Likewise, people harm the prophets who lived for a long time. Salt and light.
You are the salt which the earth was made with. But suppose that the salt had lost its saltiness. How could it be made salty again? It would not be good for anything anymore. They would throw it out. They would walk on it.
You are the light of the world, a city set on a hill cannot be hidden.
Also, people don't light a lamp and put it under a bowl. Instead, they put it on its stand. Then that illuminates everyone in the house.
Similarly, let your light shine before others. Then they will see the good things you do. And they will praise your Father in heaven. Jesus makes clear the full meaning of the law.
Let no one suppose that I have agreed to disappear from what is written in the Law or in the Prophets, but rather I have agreed to give the full meaning of what is written.
Here is what I am about to tell you is the truth. Heaven and earth will pass away, but not the smallest letter or the smallest part of a letter will pass from the law. And the smallest stroke of a pen will not disappear from the law until everything is complete.
Do not break even some of the least of the commands. And do not teach others how to break them. For if you do, you will be called the least of the most important person in the kingdom of heaven. But, do and teach these commands. Then, you will be called the most important person in the kingdom of heaven.
Here is what I say to you. You must be more righteous than the Pharisees and teachers of the law. If you are not, you will not enter the kingdom of heaven. You have heard that it was said, 'You shall not murder.'
I have heard what was said to the people who lived long ago. It was said to them: "You shall not commit murder." (Exodus 20:13) Anyone who commits murder will be judged for it.
But here is what I tell you. Do not be angry with your brother. Anyone who is angry with his brother will be judged. Again, anyone who says to his brother, 'Come here,' must be judged in the Sanhedrin. But anyone who says, 'You fool!' will be in danger of the fire of hell.
Let's look, we will present our gift at the altar. And let's not forget that our brother has something against you.
Put your gift before the altar. First, go and be reconciled to your brother; then come and offer your gift.
