The wicked pursue all these things. Your Father in heaven knows you need them.
But first seek the kingdom of God. Do what He wants you to do. Then you will also be given all those other things.
So don't worry about tomorrow. Tomorrow will worry about itself. Every day has enough trouble of its own.
It is better to judge others.
Do not judge others, and you will not be judged.
You will be judged by the same standard by which you judge others. You will be measured by the same measure by which you measure others.
تَنْظُرُ إِلَى الْبُقْعَةِ مِنْ سَاوْدْزٍ فِي عَيْنِ صَدِيقِكَ. وَلَكِنَّكَ لَا تُبَالِي بِالْقِطْعَةِ مِنْ الْخَشَبَةِ فِي عَيْنِكَ. الترجمة الصوتية: "You look at the bit of sawdust in your friend's eye. But you pay no attention to the piece of wood in your own eye." هذه الترجمة تلتزم بالمعنى الأصلي وتهدف إلى أن تكون مفهومة في سياق اللغة العربية الفصحى الحديثة.
How can you say to your friend, "Let me take the splinter of wood out of your eye"? How can you say this when there is a piece of wood in your own eye?
