Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.
"Can you discern their true nature through their actions? 'Do people gather grapes from thorny bushes? Do they pick figs from thistles?'"
Likewise, every good tree bears good fruit. But a corrupt tree bears corrupt fruit.
A good tree does not bear bad fruit. And a bad tree does not bear good fruit.
Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down. It is thrown into the fire.
You can distinguish every tree by its fruit.
Not everyone who says to me, 'Lord, Lord,' will enter the kingdom of heaven. For the one who does the will of my Father who is in heaven, they will enter.
Many will say to me on that day, 'Lord, Lord, did we not prophesy in your name? Did we not cast out demons in your name? Did we not perform many miracles in your name?'
Then I will tell them clearly, "I never knew you. Away from me, you evildoers!" The builders, the wise and the foolish.
Therefore, everyone who hears my words and puts them into practice is like a wise man who built his house on the rock.
Rain falls. Water rises. Winds blow and strike against that house. But it does not fall. Rather, it is built upon the rock.
But everyone who hears my words and does not put them into practice is like the foolish one. He built his house on sand.
The rain falls. The water rises. The wind blows and beats on that house. And it falls with a loud crack."
Jesus finished all that he had to say. The groups were amazed at his teaching.
Teach as if you have authority. He did not speak as their listening was to their imams.
Jesus healed a man who was suffering from a skin disease.
Jesus came down from the mountainside. Large crowds followed him.
A man who was suffering from a skin disease came and knelt down before Jesus. He said, "Lord, if you are willing to make me 'clean,' then you can do it."
Jesus stretched out his hand and touched the man. He said, "I am willing to do this. Be 'clean'!" Immediately, the man was healed of his skin disease.
Then he said to him, "Do not tell anyone, go and make yourself known to the priest, and present the gift that Moses commanded. For it will be a witness against them." A Romanian said, "He has believed in this!"
When Jesus entered Capernaum, a Roman centurion came to him. The centurion asked Jesus for help.
"My master," he said, "my servant is lying in the house and cannot move. He is suffering terribly."
Jesus said, "I will go and heal him."
The captain replied, "Sir, I am not qualified to receive you in my house. But, all you have to do is speak the word, and my servant will be healed."
I myself am a man under authority. And I have soldiers under my command who obey my orders. I say to this one, 'Go,' and he goes. I say to that one, 'Come,' and he comes. I say to my servant, 'Do this,' and he does it."
When Jesus heard this, he was amazed. He said to those who were following him, "What I am about to tell you is the truth. I have not found anyone in Israel whose faith is as strong as this."
I tell you that many will come from the east and the west. They will take their places at the feast in the kingdom of heaven. They will be seated with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.
But those who think that they are from the kingdom are thrown out, into the darkness. There they strive and are... "
Then Jesus said to the centurions, "Go! It will happen as you have believed." And his servant was healed at that same hour. Jesus heals many people.
When Jesus came to Peter's house, he saw Peter's mother-in-law lying in bed. She was suffering from a fever.
Jesus touched her hand, and the fever left her. She got up and began to wait for him.
And in the evening, many who were possessed by demons were brought to Jesus. He cast out the spirits with a word. And He healed all the sick.
He did this to make what the prophet Isaiah said would come true. He said, "He suffered the things we should suffer. He took on his body the diseases we should have carried." (Isaiah 53:4) The Cost of Following Jesus
Jesus saw the crowd surrounding him. Therefore, he gave his disciples orders to go to the other side of the Sea of Galilee.
Then a man came to him who was teaching writing. He said, "O teacher, I will not follow you wherever you go."
Jesus answered, "The foxes have holes. The birds of the sky have nests. But the Son of Man has no place to lay his head."
My master, first let me go and bury my father.
But Jesus said to him, "Follow Me. Let the dead bury their dead." Jesus calms the storm.
Jesus entered a boat. His disciples followed him.
Suddenly, a terrible storm came upon the lake. The waves beat against the boat. But Jesus was sleeping.
The statement and they woke him up. So they said, "Lord! Save us! Indeed, we are the victors!"
He replied, "Your faith is too small! Why are you so afraid?" Then Jesus got up and commanded the winds and waves to stop. And immediately the storm subsided and became perfectly calm.
The disciples were amazed. They asked, "What kind of man is this? Even the winds and the sea obey him!" Jesus healed two men who were controlled by demons.
Jesus arrived on the other side of the lake, in the region of the Gadarenes. Two men who were possessed by demons met him. They had come from the tombs. The men were so violent that no one could travel on that road.
"Sons of God, what do you want from us?" they cried out. "Have you come here to punish us before the time of judgment for us arrives?"
Not so very far away, a large herd of pigs was feeding.
The demons begged Jesus, "If you drive us out, send us into the herd of pigs."
Jesus said to them, "Go!" And the demons came out of the men and entered the pigs. The entire herd rushed down the steep hill. They rushed into the lake, where they drowned.
Those who were tending the pigs fled. They went into the town and reported all this. They told the people what had happened to the men who were possessed by demons.
Then the entire population of the town went out to meet Jesus, peace be upon him. And when they saw him, they begged him to leave their region.
Jesus healed a man who could not walk.
Jesus got into a boat. Then he went to the other side of the lake and came to his own town.
Some men came to him with a man who could not walk. He was lying on a bed. Jesus saw that they had faith. He said to the man, "Do not lose hope, my son. Your sins are forgiven."
Then some of them said to each other, "This one is saying something great."
Jesus knew what they were thinking. So He said, "Why do you have evil thoughts in your hearts?"
Which is easier to say, "Your sins are forgiven"? Or to say, "Rise up and walk"?
I want you to know that the man's son has power over the earth to forgive sins. Then he spoke to the man who had not walked. "Rise up," he said. "Take your mat and go to your house."
The man got up and returned to his house.
And when the people saw it, they marveled, and glorified God, which had given such power unto men. Jesus Chooseth Matthew
As Jesus continued on from there, he saw a man named Matthew. He was sitting in the tax collector's booth. "Follow me," Jesus said to him. Matthew got up and followed Jesus.
Later Jesus was having dinner at Matthew's house. Many tax collectors and "sinners" came and ate with Jesus and his disciples.
The Pharisees saw this. And they asked the disciples, "Why does your teacher eat with tax collectors and 'sinners'?"
Jesus came to that realization. He said, "Those who are well don't need a doctor. The sick do."
Jesus is asked about fasting. 'The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Why do your disciples not fast, while the disciples of the Pharisees do fast? John's disciples also fast, and the Pharisees do too." Jesus answered them, "How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while he is with them? As long as they have the bridegroom with them, they cannot fast. But the days will come when the bridegroom is taken away from them; then they will fast in those days. No one sews a patch of unshrunk cloth onto an old garment; otherwise, the new patch will pull away from the old garment, and the tear will be worse. Likewise, no one puts new wine into old wineskins; otherwise, the new wine will burst the skins, and both the wine and the wineskins will be ruined. But new wine must be put into new wineskins, and both are preserved." '
One day, the disciples of John came to Jesus and said, "We and the Pharisees fast regularly, but your disciples do not fast."
Jesus answered, "How can the guests of the bridegroom mourn while he is with them? The time will come when the bridegroom is taken from them; then they will fast."
People do not sew a patch of new cloth onto old clothing. The new piece will pull away from the old garment. This will make the tear worse.
