Listen! Here is the meaning of the story of the farmer.
The people hear the message about the kingdom, but they do not understand. Then the devil comes. He steals what was given in their hearts. Those people are like a seed planted in a road.
Another group received the seed that fell on the rocky places. They are the ones who hear the message and immediately receive it with joy.
But they have no roots. Therefore, they last only for a little while. They quickly fall away from faith when trouble or suffering comes because of the message.
Other worries accompanied them, always: the anxieties that go with it, and the false promises of making money. These worries took hold of the opportunity and prevented it from bearing fruit.
"But others also, to whom the seed that had fallen on good soil. Those are the ones who hear the word, and understand it. They bring forth a crop, 100 or 60 or 30 fold of what the farmer planted." The Parable of the Weeds
Jesus told the crowd another story. "This is what the Kingdom of Heaven is like," Jesus said. "A man planted a good seed in his field."
