"No," the owner replied. "While you are pulling out the weeds, you might pull out the wheat along with it."
Let them sleep together until the harvest. Then I will tell the workers what to do. Here is what I will tell them. First, gather the weeds. Bind them into bundles to be burned. Then, gather the wheat. Bring it to my storage.' 'Stories of the Mustard Seed and the Yeast'
Jesus told the crowd another parable. He said, "The kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed. Someone took the seed and planted it in a field."
It is the smallest of all your seeds. But when it grows, it is the largest of all the garden plants. It becomes a tree. The birds come and rest in its branches.
Jesus told them another parable. "The kingdom of heaven is like yeast," he said. "A woman took yeast and mixed it into a large amount of flour. The yeast worked its way through the entire dough."
Jesus spoke all these things to the crowd in parables. He did not speak to them without a parable.
The prophecy of the prophet was thus fulfilled. For he had said, "I will open my mouth in parables; I will utter dark sayings from of old." (Psalm 78:2) Jesus explains the parable of the weeds.
