The Kingdom of Heaven is like treasure hidden in a field, which a man found and hid; then he goes and sells all that he has and buys that field.
And once again, he likened the Kingdom of Heaven to a merchant who was seeking fine pearls.
He found one that was very valuable. So he went away and sold everything he had. And he bought that pearl. The Parable of the Net
Again, the Kingdom of Heaven is like a net. It was cast into the lake. It gathered all kinds of fish.
When it was full, the fishermen drew it to the shore. Then they sat down and gathered the good fish into baskets. As for the bad fish, they threw them away.
This is how it will be on the Day of Judgment. The angels will come. They will separate the people who did what is wrong from those who did what is right.
They will throw the wicked people into the burning oven. There the wicked will tremble and gnash their teeth.
