When dinner was near, the disciples came to him. "Nothing is here," they said. "It is near to dinner time. Send the groups in several. They can go and buy some food in the villages."
Jesus answered, "They do not need to go away. Give them something to eat."
"We have five loaves of bread and two fish," they answered.
"Bring them here to me," he said.
Then Jesus instructed the people to sit down on the grass. He took five loaves and two fish. He looked up to heaven and gave thanks. He broke the loaves into pieces. Then He gave them to the disciples. And the disciples gave them to the people.
They all ate and were satisfied. And he selected 12 baskets of the leftovers.
